# Code architecture

- Single human entry: `python code/run.py --config code/configs/experiments/<name>.yaml [--models a,b@variant
  --split-seeds 41 --tag-suffix X --device cuda]`. Runner for this round: `foundation_cross_subject`
  (`code/experiments/cross_subject_protocols.py`) + `code/training/e2e_trainer.py`.
- Model aliases `name@variant` resolve through `code/models/model_specs.py` (single source of parameters);
  unknown aliases must raise. This round's entries: `eegnex`, `eegnet_official`, `seegnex@{hplif, s_lif,
  s_plif, s_hplif, s_hplif_afe, s_hplif_spk, s_hplif_noinit, s_hplif_causal, s_hplif_hard, s_hplif_noreg,
  s_hplif_all}`, `seegnet@plif`.
- Model-specific training behaviour goes into hooks (`uses_custom_loss` / `training_step` /
  `after_optimizer_step`), never a forked trainer. `code/training/trainer.py` is frozen. All models return
  `{logits, features, confidence}`; spiking models additionally implement `describe()` and `pop_spike_stats()`.
- New model = `code/models/<name>/` + `code/configs/models/<name>.yaml` + registration in
  `code/models/registry.py` + a test in `tests/models/`. New experiment grid = edit
  `scripts/make_snn_configs.py` and regenerate; do not hand-edit the 24 `snn_*.yaml` (6 of them are the main run).
- Deprecated models (`s4erp_adv`, `atcnet_adv`, `dualcd_s4_pos`, in-house `eegnet`, `cap_eegnet`) and the
  cross-session-era modules (`code/tta/`, `code/methods/`, phase runners) stay in the tree: `docs/RESULTS_TRUTH.md`
  numbers and `tests/tta` depend on them.
- `PROJECT_ROOT` is derived from `__file__` (`code/utils/paths.py`), so the repo works from any path.
